    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "7a424791-4ca0-390b-824b-6dcc8e4f745c",
                "word": "ascus",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6eadaa19-8305-4289-8860-8022b17ab853",
                        "entry_id": "7a424791-4ca0-390b-824b-6dcc8e4f745c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "asci"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1bc3bfc9-d498-37f4-ad82-0bc57aff6e0f",
                        "entry_id": "7a424791-4ca0-390b-824b-6dcc8e4f745c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A sac-shaped cell present in ascomycete fungi; it is a reproductive cell in which meiosis and an additional cell division produce eight spores."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "618543c9-7ac8-43d8-bf65-cc4768bd106c",
                                "sense_id": "1bc3bfc9-d498-37f4-ad82-0bc57aff6e0f",
                                "text": "The one important character which distinguishes the Ascomycetes from all other fungi is the ascus (plural, asci). This is a sac-like structure in which ascospores are formed following karyogamy and meiosis."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9d8f7fc8-f317-4ee0-bc16-93cf5914043c",
                        "source_entry_id": "7a424791-4ca0-390b-824b-6dcc8e4f745c",
                        "source_sense_id": "1bc3bfc9-d498-37f4-ad82-0bc57aff6e0f",
                        "source_sense_description": "a sac-shaped cell present in ascomycete fungi",
                        "target_lang_word": "asque",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "asque",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8373f340-4421-3284-b222-26823a6aa42a",
                                        "entry_id": "e5bf2047-f766-3b38-8a63-56b2b25dfe8c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Cellule reproductrice des champignons ascomycètes (dont font partie les truffes, les morilles et les pézizes) en forme de sac généralement allongé qui contient le plus fréquemment 8 spores (spécifiquement nommées ascospores) après la méiose. L'asque s'oppose à la baside des basidiomycètes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1729b968-0701-4f7c-97d1-a41457f8f093",
                                                "sense_id": "8373f340-4421-3284-b222-26823a6aa42a",
                                                "text": "Parmi les ressemblances, certaines relèvent du lien évolutif entre organismes : les ressemblances qui sont heritees d'un ancetre commun. C'est ainsi que !'ensemble des Ascomycetes ont des asques, hérités d'un ancêtre commun qui en possédait."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5a26086-ce67-4eec-ae44-9177a91c617d",
                                                "sense_id": "8373f340-4421-3284-b222-26823a6aa42a",
                                                "text": "Quant aux asques, elles se développent suivant le processus ordinaire."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "da11099b-408b-4871-ae79-4797deb2e366",
                        "source_entry_id": "7a424791-4ca0-390b-824b-6dcc8e4f745c",
